"verdict": "BLOCK",
"p0": [
{
"title": "`join`/`causalJoin` are reclassified as control operations in every profile, removing them from application delivery, the blueprint fold and operation admission under `creator-trusted-v1`",
"evidence": "`packages/node/src/v3-live.ts:3501` defines `isControlOperation` as `action === AUTHOR_FENCE_ACTION || action === \"causalJoin\" || action === \"join\"` with no `settlementProfileFor` gate, and every consumer added by this GREEN is likewise ungated: ingress `:3966` skips `reserveOperation`, `:4040` adds the digest to `registration.controlVertices`, and `:4051` `if (controlOperation) return true;` returns before the `onAdmittedVertex` delivery at `:4060`; local issue `:6549` adds to `controlVertices` and `:6559` `if (currentRegistration(registration) && !controlOperation)` skips the sink; recovery `:5613`/`:5836` add to `controlVertices` and `:5834` skips reservation; and `applicationProjectionVertices` at `:7548`/`:7561` now skips and deletes every `controlVertices` member from the map handed to `foldBlueprintEpoch` (`:7576`), where the pre-GREEN predicate was `isAuthorFenceOperation`, which is unreachable outside settlement because `:3904` and `:5580` reject fences under a legacy profile. `join` is a real reducer-backed application operation, not a Node-only structural one: `packages/node/src/v3-live.ts:6250` rejects it locally only when `values.length > 1`, `:6254` requires a registered reducer, and `examples/grid/src/v3-zone.ts:1272` and `examples/v3-chat/src/index.ts:499` use `{action:\"join\", ...}` as the room `bootstrapOperation`, with `examples/grid/src/v3-zone.ts:1312` building the entire zone roster from the accepted `join` operation. `causalJoin` is issued by the Node itself for frontier reduction at `packages/node/src/v3-live.ts:6701` in all profiles.",
"impact": "Breaks `creator-trusted-v1`, which the accepted design requires to be byte-for-byte unchanged (`.logs/d110c-0c1f5b0r-design-3a156aca/design.md:546`). Two independent product failures: (a) the application sink never receives `join`/`causalJoin`, so the room's roster/bootstrap projection is empty on every peer that learns the vertex over gossip; (b) the closed epoch fold silently omits those vertices, so the derived commitment diverges from any peer or replay running the parent commit, and the reserved-ABI enforcement that `reserveOperation` performed for `causalJoin` is gone. Two retained legacy suites that were excluded from the 87/87 gate encode exactly this: `tests/phase-3f-b-v3-frontier-reduction-red.test.ts:37` (`expectEveryIssuedVertexDelivered` asserts `admittedDigests` equals every issued digest, including the `causalJoin` vertices at `:62` and `:81-84`) and `:159-168` (`causalJoin: \"missing\" | \"altered-abi\"` must make issuance fail, which only `reserveOperation` enforced).",
"repair": "Gate the join/causalJoin arm of `isControlOperation` on `settlementProfileFor(payload.trust.trust.profileId) === \"v1\"` (or introduce a separate `isSettlementControlOperation` and keep `isAuthorFenceOperation` at the ungated sites), so legacy ingress, local issue, recovery, reservation, sink delivery and `applicationProjectionVertices` keep pre-GREEN behavior for `join`/`causalJoin`; then add `tests/phase-3f-b-v3-frontier-reduction-red.test.ts`, `tests/phase-3f-b-chat-zone-causal-join-red.test.ts` and `tests/phase-3f-c-v3-application-batching-red.test.ts` to the retained gate and re-record GREEN."
}
],
"p1": [
{
"title": "Displaced `authorSequence === 0` rows are now skipped for every displaced source, not only cross-object imports",
"evidence": "`packages/node/src/v3-live.ts:6942-6948`. The pre-GREEN guard was `!historical && crossSource !== undefined && (row.authorSequence === 0 || digest === crossSource.activationVertexDigest)`; GREEN moved `crossSource !== undefined` inside so the clause reads `!historical && (classified.row.authorSequence === 0 || (crossSource !== undefined && ...))`. `crossSource` is `undefined` whenever `registration.displacedSource?.issuanceStore === undefined` (`:6843`), i.e. the ordinary same-store legacy/latched displaced source and every settlement drain, since `readSettlementSources` (`:8635`) never supplies a cross-object store.",
"impact": "Legacy: a non-creator writer whose slot 0 is an ordinary application vertex (not the creator's pinned-genesis bootstrap, which classifies `pinned-genesis`/historical and is unaffected) loses that row from the rebase outbox after a close — silent work loss where the parent commit surfaced it. Settlement: the design requires every own row above `terminalThrough` to become a plan entry (`design.md:192-207`, `:214-228`); a null-boundary or returning author's displaced slot-0 row is dropped before it can be dispositioned, so the plan is completed and fenced while that source is neither expired, rebased nor transformed.",
"repair": "Restore the `crossSource !== undefined &&` conjunct on the whole clause so slot 0 is only excluded for cross-object activation imports, and add a focused case for a displaced slot-0 own row under both `creator-trusted-v1` and `creator-trusted-settlement-v1`."
},
{
"title": "Recovery drops the issued/outbox cross-read under the settlement profile, removing the corruption latch with no replacement",
"evidence": "`packages/node/src/v3-live.ts:5648-5665`: `let issuedRow = row; if (settlementProfileFor(payload.trust.trust.profileId) !== \"v1\") { ...readIssued... }`. Under `v1` no `readIssued` call is made, so nothing checks that the outbox row matches the durable issued record. The skip is unforced: `outboxRowSnapshot` was widened at `:4229-4231` to accept `ISSUE_COMMIT_WITH_PLAN_EFFECT_KEYS` and drops `planEffect` from the returned snapshot (`:4266-4273`), and `authenticatedOutboxRow` at `:6820` still performs the identical cross-read unconditionally for the same plan-linked rows and passes. `issuedRow` is also dead after the change — it is assigned at `:5648`/`:5664` and never read, since `classifyPlaneVertex` at `:5668-5680` consumes `row`.",
"impact": "Under `creator-trusted-settlement-v1`, a divergent or half-written outbox/issued pair recovers instead of failing closed with `\"v3 recovery issued record does not match\"`. The design explicitly relies on `readIssued` latching corruption (`design.md:286-290`), and this slice removes that latch precisely on the profile that introduces the new atomic `planEffect` writes.",
"repair": "Delete the profile branch and run the cross-read in both profiles (or state a concrete reason the settlement path cannot), and remove the now-dead `issuedRow` local. Add a focused case where the settlement outbox row and issued record disagree and assert `issuance-rejected`."
},
{
"title": "`ISSUANCE_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN` early return preempts the terminal branch, so an ambiguous terminal publish no longer latches the terminal state",
"evidence": "`packages/node/src/v3-live.ts:6427-6429` returns `internalLocalIssueFailure(\"issuance-rejected\", \"v3 local issue transaction outcome is unknown\")` with no terminal intent, ahead of the pre-existing `:6430-6436` branch that returned `\"outcome-unknown\"` when `requireTerminalAuthorization && terminalTransactionStarted`. `terminalTransactionStarted` is set at `:6395` immediately before the terminal `transactIssue`, so an `ISSUANCE_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN` throw from that call now takes the new path. `terminalIssueFailure` at `:7335-7342` maps a missing `terminalIntent` to `\"absent\"`, and `publishTerminalIssue` at `:7391` only sets `registration.terminalState = \"terminal\"` when the intent is `\"outcome-unknown\"`.",
"impact": "A terminal migration-activation issue whose durable outcome is genuinely unknown is now reported as an ordinary rejection and the plane stays `\"transition\"` instead of latching `\"terminal\"`, so further local issues are accepted against a possibly-committed terminal vertex. This affects both profiles and regresses D.110c terminal-transition fail-closed behavior; no test in the repository exercises either message (`\"v3 terminal issue transaction outcome is unknown\"` and `\"v3 local issue transaction outcome is unknown\"` appear only in `packages/node/src/v3-live.ts`), and retained `tests/phase-3h-v3-terminal-transition-red.test.ts` only covers sink dispositions (`:58-70`).",
"repair": "Move the new early return below the `requireTerminalAuthorization && terminalTransactionStarted` branch, or make it carry `\"outcome-unknown\"` when that condition holds, and add a focused case that throws `{code:\"ISSUANCE_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN\"}` from the terminal `transactIssue` and asserts `terminalIntent: \"outcome-unknown\"` plus a latched terminal state."
}
],
