"title": "Control classification moved from operation-derived to a digest set that is not populated for vertices seeded from the recovery payload graph",
"evidence": "`packages/node/src/v3-live.ts:5429-5451` seeds `closeVertices` from `copyCloseVertices(payload.vertices)` and creates an empty `controlVertices` set; only journal replay (`:5613`), outbox recovery (`:5836`), ingress (`:4040`) and local issue (`:6549`) add digests. `applicationProjectionVertices` (`:7548`, `:7561`) now keys exclusively off that set, where the pre-GREEN code re-derived control status from `vertex.operation` via `isAuthorFenceOperation`. Any control vertex present in `payload.vertices` is therefore folded as an application vertex.",
"owner": "f5b0c/f5b (settlement close/fold integration)",
"disposition": "Defer with reason — currently latent because `payload.vertices` carries the anchor (and `reclaimV3RuntimeKernel:3266` clears `controlVertices` alongside the anchor-only reset), but re-derive control status from the operation when seeding `controlVertices`, or assert the invariant, before a retained graph can carry a fence."
