"title": "`issueAuthorFence` trusts the durable settlement plan shape instead of capturing it with the file's strict closed-record discipline",
"evidence": "`packages/node/src/v3-live.ts:6586-6600`: only `readSettlementPlan` is wrapped in `try`; the subsequent `plan.fenceSequence !== null` and `plan.entries.some((entry) => entry.disposition === \"manual-review\")` read the store value directly, with no `snapshotClosedRecord`/`denseArray` capture and no check that `plan.scope` matches `registration.issuanceScope`. A plan whose `entries` is not an array throws out of the enqueued task rather than returning a typed `V3LocalIssueResult`.",
"owner": "f5b0c (room plan building) with the f5b0s store contract",
"disposition": "Fix now — capture the plan with the same exact-key/dense-array discipline used for every other external input in this file and return `issuance-rejected` on a malformed plan; the fence refusal semantics themselves are correct."
},
{
"title": "Retained gate selection does not cover the legacy paths this slice modified",
"evidence": "`.logs/d110c-0c1f5b0b-green-93585bf3/commands.md:18-27` records six retained files (settlement codec, settlement plan store, authorized recovery, creator close, rebase outbox, terminal transition). None exercises `join`/`causalJoin` under a legacy profile, the displaced slot-0 path, or an ambiguous terminal issuance outcome, which are exactly the three behaviors changed at `packages/node/src/v3-live.ts:3501`, `:6944` and `:6427`. The focused suite touches `join`/`causalJoin` only via `settlementProfile: true` (`tests/phase-6b-d110c-0c1f5b0b-node-red.test.ts:308-331`).",
"owner": "this slice (D.110c-0c1f5b0b) on re-record",
