"summary": "RED is genuinely causal (tests-only `f7f693b7`, 6 controls pass / 21 product obligations fail, signed linear custody `882a3dc1 → 93585bf3 → 9b02f9c2`), and GREEN does close the settlement obligations it targets: strict exact-shape settlement advance capture, a dedicated fence issuer that reads the durable plan and refuses absent/manual-review/already-linked plans, a derived rather than caller-supplied fence `planEffect` bound to the issuance lineage, settlement-only `planEffect` with `V3LocalIssueInput` (v3-live.ts:517) unchanged, legacy fence ingress rejected before journal/graph/reservation work, published-and-pending own-row scanning, and an internal protocol-v3 subpath that does not leak `verifyReceivedVertex` from the root (public.ts exports 12 symbols without it) with an exactly matching, correctly ordered Vite alias. The partial older-row path is represented honestly: any-anchor authentication requires a validated `{currentEpoch, admissionEpoch, terminalThrough}` context, terminal and old-incarnation rows are filtered before surfacing (v3-live.ts:6892-6901), and f5b0c/f5b is correctly named as the owner of threading the verified frontier. No wire, protobuf, schema, dependency, threshold, campaign, room, pruning or creator-integration change entered the slice and no design stop rule fired. It nevertheless blocks: the close-graph split was implemented by making `isControlOperation` treat `join`/`causalJoin` as controls in every profile, so under `creator-trusted-v1` those vertices are no longer delivered to the application sink, no longer reserved, and are deleted from the blueprint fold projection — silently emptying the room's `join`-carried roster and diverging the closed epoch commitment, which the design forbids and which two legacy suites omitted from the retained gate already assert. Three further regressions ride along: displaced slot-0 rows are now dropped for all same-store sources (legacy work loss and an undispositioned settlement plan source), recovery drops the issued/outbox cross-read under settlement with no replacement despite the identical check still passing in `authenticatedOutboxRow`, and the new `ISSUANCE_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN` early return strips the `outcome-unknown` terminal intent so an ambiguous terminal publish stops latching the terminal state. The recorded evidence is honest and reproducible, but the 87/87 retained selection does not cover any of these paths, so it does not support the byte-for-byte legacy-unchanged claim."
}
